<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I0bab6385508793d7366c0e48524343d4b0d14a28" commit="33999342feccdf5406cab05397ab777afe7b8e2d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: KEYS: Fix race between key destruction and finding a keyring by name  There appears to be a race between:   (1) key_gc_unused_keys() which frees key-&gt;security and then calls      keyring_destroy() to unlink the name from the name list   (2) find_keyring_by_name() which calls key_permission(), thus accessing      key-&gt;security, on a key before checking to see whether the key usage is 0      (ie. the key is dead and might be cleaned up).  Fix this by calling -&gt;destroy() before cleaning up the core key data - including key-&gt;security.  BUG=chromium:542341 TEST=build/boot on amd64-generic  Reported-by: Petr Matousek &lt;pmatouse@redhat.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David Howells &lt;dhowells@redhat.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 94c4554ba07adbdde396748ee7ae01e86cf2d8d7) Signed-off-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I0bab6385508793d7366c0e48524343d4b0d14a28 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/315613 Commit-Ready: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kees Cook &lt;keescook@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="315613" owner_email="sonnyrao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/13/315613/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1d8591cfc63fab290d4dafa3cacd42e28865dc6d" commit="f5a9abe7f4a2fc807dd3f51ed7f9f5bcef5a1331" commit_message="UPSTREAM: KEYS: Fix crash when attempt to garbage collect an uninstantiated keyring  The following sequence of commands:      i=`keyctl add user a a @s`     keyctl request2 keyring foo bar @t     keyctl unlink $i @s  tries to invoke an upcall to instantiate a keyring if one doesn't already exist by that name within the user's keyring set.  However, if the upcall fails, the code sets keyring-&gt;type_data.reject_error to -ENOKEY or some other error code.  When the key is garbage collected, the key destroy function is called unconditionally and keyring_destroy() uses list_empty() on keyring-&gt;type_data.link - which is in a union with reject_error. Subsequently, the kernel tries to unlink the keyring from the keyring names list - which oopses like this:   BUG: unable to handle kernel paging request at 00000000ffffff8a  IP: [&lt;ffffffff8126e051&gt;] keyring_destroy+0x3d/0x88  ...  Workqueue: events key_garbage_collector  ...  RIP: 0010:[&lt;ffffffff8126e051&gt;] keyring_destroy+0x3d/0x88  RSP: 0018:ffff88003e2f3d30  EFLAGS: 00010203  RAX: 00000000ffffff82 RBX: ffff88003bf1a900 RCX: 0000000000000000  RDX: 0000000000000000 RSI: 000000003bfc6901 RDI: ffffffff81a73a40  RBP: ffff88003e2f3d38 R08: 0000000000000152 R09: 0000000000000000  R10: ffff88003e2f3c18 R11: 000000000000865b R12: ffff88003bf1a900  R13: 0000000000000000 R14: ffff88003bf1a908 R15: ffff88003e2f4000  ...  CR2: 00000000ffffff8a CR3: 000000003e3ec000 CR4: 00000000000006f0  ...  Call Trace:   [&lt;ffffffff8126c756&gt;] key_gc_unused_keys.constprop.1+0x5d/0x10f   [&lt;ffffffff8126ca71&gt;] key_garbage_collector+0x1fa/0x351   [&lt;ffffffff8105ec9b&gt;] process_one_work+0x28e/0x547   [&lt;ffffffff8105fd17&gt;] worker_thread+0x26e/0x361   [&lt;ffffffff8105faa9&gt;] ? rescuer_thread+0x2a8/0x2a8   [&lt;ffffffff810648ad&gt;] kthread+0xf3/0xfb   [&lt;ffffffff810647ba&gt;] ? kthread_create_on_node+0x1c2/0x1c2   [&lt;ffffffff815f2ccf&gt;] ret_from_fork+0x3f/0x70   [&lt;ffffffff810647ba&gt;] ? kthread_create_on_node+0x1c2/0x1c2  Note the value in RAX.  This is a 32-bit representation of -ENOKEY.  The solution is to only call -&gt;destroy() if the key was successfully instantiated.  BUG=chromium:542341 TEST=build/boot on amd64-generic  Reported-by: Dmitry Vyukov &lt;dvyukov@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David Howells &lt;dhowells@redhat.com&gt; Tested-by: Dmitry Vyukov &lt;dvyukov@google.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit f05819df10d7b09f6d1eb6f8534a8f68e5a4fe61) Signed-off-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I1d8591cfc63fab290d4dafa3cacd42e28865dc6d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/315614 Commit-Ready: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kees Cook &lt;keescook@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="315614" owner_email="sonnyrao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/14/315614/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I846b1baef0b0cba9112e8e50dbeea98979d82a10" commit="db8a6c7542896a69f8e9a21339d04ae8d9972df6" commit_message="UPSTREAM: KEYS: Don't permit request_key() to construct a new keyring  If request_key() is used to find a keyring, only do the search part - don't do the construction part if the keyring was not found by the search.  We don't really want keyrings in the negative instantiated state since the rejected/negative instantiation error value in the payload is unioned with keyring metadata.  Now the kernel gives an error:   request_key(&quot;keyring&quot;, &quot;#selinux,bdekeyring&quot;, &quot;keyring&quot;, KEY_SPEC_USER_SESSION_KEYRING) = -1 EPERM (Operation not permitted)  BUG=chromium:542341 TEST=build/boot amd64-generic, run test program from bug and verify kernel   doesn't crash  Signed-off-by: David Howells &lt;dhowells@redhat.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 911b79cde95c7da0ec02f48105358a36636b7a71) Signed-off-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I846b1baef0b0cba9112e8e50dbeea98979d82a10 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/315615 Commit-Ready: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kees Cook &lt;keescook@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="315615" owner_email="sonnyrao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/15/315615/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2188d957d2640d9d25d3ed9d782297e72a7bf3ac" commit="a82f46e67d6420e81a638e9bc693efa107e7b0a3" commit_message="init: remove WP screw bypass for block_devmode  Currently, removing the WP screw bypasses the block_devmode check for recovery mode images.  Remove that check.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48230 BRANCH=none TEST=manual   1. Enable developer mode   2. Boot a recovery image with an unsigned rootfs.  It should work.   3. crossystem block_devmode=1   4. Reboot.  Recovery image is blocked.   5. Remove the WP screw and reboot.  Recovery image is still blocked.  Change-Id: I2188d957d2640d9d25d3ed9d782297e72a7bf3ac Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/315800 Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="315800" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/initramfs" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/initramfs" ref="refs/changes/00/315800/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic92666bd56eaaf16b2f01c972e857f9e8254cd13" commit="ab03dcdee5229673756f517ee069f98f84c997c7" commit_message="init: remove WP screw bypass for block_devmode  Currently, removing the WP screw bypasses the block_devmode check. Remove that check.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48229 BRANCH=none TEST=manual   1. Enable developer mode   2. Boot to a root shell   3. crossystem block_devmode=1   4. Reboot.  Dev mode is blocked.   5. Remove the WP screw and reboot.  Dev mode is still blocked.  Change-Id: Ic92666bd56eaaf16b2f01c972e857f9e8254cd13 Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/315732 Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="315732" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/32/315732/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7703.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>